      "architectureDecision": "The universal generic ConPTY input-mode claim was removed. ConPTY does not expose the child's DEC pointer/focus negotiation, and process-local stdout interception cannot cover direct descriptor/native writes or descendants. The supported contract is capability-based: opaque children fail closed, while an explicitly registered provider backed by the application's production mode state may publish authoritative revision-bound evidence."
